R2825 / D-20261116-13 value-domain assertion shared by the four price faces
================================================================================
Dispatch: D-20261116-13 to @BigDomain, deadline 2026-11-17 12:00.
Ruling text: every --check green must carry at least one VALUE-DOMAIN assertion
(price, entitlement, period or quota compared against the catalog, not
structural self-consistency); the four price faces must gain them and be green
together; it must be one reusable module rather than four copies.

WHAT WAS MEASURED AT OPEN (not guessed)
---------------------------------------
payment_gate_report.check() already compared landed product rows against
src/sandbox/pay/config.json (R2817, AC-PAYGB10/11).
money_path_demo.check(), membership_face.gate() and membership_benefit_report
.verify() carried ONLY structural checks: "landed == fresh derivation",
"size == disk", "cycle shape is not self-contradictory". A chain that is
consistently wrong with itself reads green - exactly what R2816 measured when
three faces printed PASS over a landed price_cent=1990 and a config reading 990.

WHAT SHIPPED
------------
tools/value_domain.py - ONE module:
  catalog(root)                 live products + tiers + both config sha256
  product_failures(rows, cat)   price_cent / channel / entitlement by value,
                                names the product and both numbers
  tier_failures(rows, cat)      period_days / monthly_credits / privileges by
                                value, names the tier
  config_drift(sha, cat)        document rendered against another config
  require_one=True              a face that compares NOTHING is RED, so
                                "structurally green" cannot pass
Four importers of that one module:
  tools/payment_gate_report.py        VD.config_drift + VD.product_failures
  tools/money_path_demo.py            VD.product_failures (price_cent)
  tools/membership_face.py            VD.product_failures + VD.tier_failures
  tools/membership_benefit_report.py  VD.tier_failures folded into AC-MBG2's
                                      condition, and the per-tier values in
                                      AC-MBG2/AC-MBG3 now come from the LIVE
                                      catalog instead of the derivation that
                                      produced the facts

CRITERIA PINNED BEFORE THE CODE (src/os/backlog.md, R2825 [PIN] row)
  AC-VD1 one module, four importers.       AC-VD2 product value assertion.
  AC-VD3 config drift.                     AC-VD4 period/quota assertion.
  AC-VD5 four faces green together.        AC-VD6 private-world red control.
  AC-VD7 reuse is machine-checked.         AC-VD8 registered in the battery.

